# Change Management Rules

## Core Principles

- Current-state docs and historical change docs must both be maintained.
- New requirements, bug fixes, refactors, and releases must not land without document traces.

## Recording Rules

- New requirements or requirement changes: update the affected workflow and knowledge docs, and create a workspace under `docs/changes/active/<change-key>/`
- Bug fixes: update affected docs and record symptom, root cause, verification, and impact inside `docs/changes/active/<change-key>/`
- Architecture or major technical changes: update `docs/workflow/02-design/README.md`, `docs/knowledge/structure/README.md`, and record an ADR
- Releases: add or update `docs/releases/vx.y.z.md`
- Before implementation: run analyze and confirm `FR / DES / TEST / T` plus the change workspace do not conflict
- After implementation: run converge and confirm real behavior, verification results, and docs align
- Once a change is done: move the workspace into `docs/changes/completed/`
- When committing: follow `docs/rules/commit-rules.md`, link the commit body to an Issue, change workspace, requirement / design / verification docs, and record modified scope, impact scope, and test status

## Lifecycle Gate

- `docs/changes/active/<change-key>/` holds only changes that are still active, blocked, or waiting for convergence.
- When tasks are complete, verification results are recorded, sync checklists are checked, and post-implementation convergence is complete, move the whole workspace into `docs/changes/completed/`; when year/month archiving is enabled, move it into `docs/changes/completed/YYYY/MM/<change-key>/`.
- Do not mark `overview.md` as `completed` while the workspace still remains under `active/`.
- If verification, documentation sync, blocker resolution, or index updates are still pending, keep the status as `needs convergence` or `blocked` and record the remaining conditions.
- After the move, update the `docs/changes/README.md` index and any commit, release, issue, or ADR references to the workspace path.

## Minimum Requirements

- Every change workspace must include background, impact scope, synced docs, and open questions
- Every bug record must include symptom, root cause, fix approach, and regression requirements
- Every release record must include added items, fixed items, breaking changes, and known issues
- Every implementation round must have an analyze conclusion before coding and a convergence result before delivery
- Every delivery must confirm completed changes no longer remain under `docs/changes/active/`
- Every commit must bind to one primary change point and trace back to the corresponding document record
